      "docsUrl": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.api_rest.meta/api_rest/",
      "dynamic": true,
      "notes": "Per-org custom fields end in __c. Lookups via SOQL query with literal spaces."
    },
    "jira": {
      "connectorKey": "uipath-atlassian-jira",
      "docsUrl": "https://developer.atlassian.com/cloud/jira/platform/rest/v2/intro/",
      "dynamic": true,
      "notes": "Custom fields keyed customfield_*. Field set depends on project + issue type (parent fields)."
    },
    "servicenow": {
      "connectorKey": "uipath-servicenow-servicenow",
      "docsUrl": "https://developer.servicenow.com/dev.do#!/reference/api/australia/rest/c_TableAPI",
      "dynamic": true,
      "notes": "Base URL already includes /api/now; Table API is versioned: /v1/table/<table>. Custom columns prefixed u_. WARNING: connector mangles = and ^ in sysparm_query (literal AND %-encoded) -> use =/^-free operators (STARTSWITH/LIKE) and refine client-side; verify the filter applied via row count. sysparm_fields/sysparm_limit honored."
    },
    "mailchimp": {
      "connectorKey": "uipath-mailchimp-mailchimp",
      "docsUrl": "https://mailchimp.com/developer/marketing/api/",
      "dynamic": true,
      "notes": "Audience (list) merge fields are per-list, keyed by tag (FNAME, LNAME, plus custom). CASCADING: the add/update-member body field set depends on list_id (a PATH param) -> author as a discovery resource (scopeFields:[list_id], path /lists/{list_id}/merge-fields?count=1000, fieldsAt:merge_fields). Discovered values go under merge_fields.<TAG>; static fields are email_address/status/email_type/vip/language)."
    },
    "outlook": {
      "connectorKey": "uipath-microsoft-outlook365",
      "docsUrl": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/api/overview?view=graph-rest-1.0",
      "dynamic": true,
      "notes": "Microsoft Graph. Base https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0; mail under /me/messages, /users/{id}/messages; calendar under /me/events. OData $filter/$select/$top/$orderby. Pagination via @odata.nextLink (follow as-is). Custom mail props via singleValueExtendedProperties/openExtensionProperties (per-tenant). immutableId vs default id quirk on messages."
    },
    "onedrive": {
      "connectorKey": "uipath-microsoft-onedrive",
      "docsUrl": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/api/overview?view=graph-rest-1.0",
      "dynamic": true,
      "notes": "Microsoft Graph (OneDrive & SharePoint). Base /v1.0. Files under /me/drive, /drives/{id}/items, /sites/{id}/drive. SharePoint list custom columns surface as listItem fields (per-list, tenant-specific). @odata.nextLink pagination, OData $filter/$expand. Path addressing /items/root:/path/to/file: vs item-id. delta query for change tracking."
    },
    "gmail": {
      "connectorKey": "uipath-google-gmail",
      "docsUrl": "https://developers.google.com/workspace/gmail/api/reference/rest",
      "dynamic": false,
      "notes": "Base https://gmail.googleapis.com/gmail/v1/users/{userId}/... ; use 'me' for userId. Fixed schema. Pagination via pageToken/nextPageToken. messages.list filters via q= Gmail search syntax (from:, subject:, is:unread, after:). Message bodies base64url-encoded in payload.parts. Raw uploads at /upload/gmail/v1/. batchModify/batchDelete take ID arrays."
    },
    "googledrive": {
      "connectorKey": "uipath-google-drive",
      "docsUrl": "https://developers.google.com/workspace/drive/api/guides/about-sdk?hl=en",
      "dynamic": false,
      "notes": "Base https://www.googleapis.com/drive/v3/; uploads at /upload/drive/v3/files (uploadType=media|multipart|resumable). Fixed schema. files.list pagination via pageToken/nextPageToken; filter via q= search syntax (mimeType=, name contains, 'PARENT_ID' in parents, trashed=false). Default fields sparse -> pass fields= to expand. Shared Drives need supportsAllDrives=true. Export Google-native docs via files/{id}/export."
    },
    "googlesheets": {
      "connectorKey": "uipath-google-sheets",
      "docsUrl": "https://developers.google.com/workspace/sheets/api/reference/rest?hl=en",
      "dynamic": true,
      "notes": "Base https://sheets.googleapis.com/v4/spreadsheets/{spreadsheetId}. Ranges use A1 notation in path, URL-encode (e.g. Sheet1!A1:C10). values.get/update/append; valueInputOption=RAW|USER_ENTERED required on writes. Multi-range via values:batchGet?ranges=...&ranges=...; structural edits via :batchUpdate. Cell contents are arbitrary user data -> no fixed column schema."
    },
    "teams": {
      "connectorKey": "uipath-microsoft-teams",
      "docsUrl": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/api/resources/teams-api-overview?view=graph-rest-1.0",
      "dynamic": false,
      "notes": "Microsoft Graph. Base /v1.0. /teams/{id}/channels/{id}/messages, /chats/{id}/messages. @odata.nextLink pagination; many message/list endpoints reject arbitrary $filter (limited OData support). Fixed schema; no tenant custom fields on core objects."
    },
    "openai": {
      "connectorKey": "uipath-openai-openai",
      "docsUrl": "https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference",
      "dynamic": false,
      "notes": "Fixed host https://api.openai.com/v1. POST /v1/chat/completions. Auth: Authorization: Bearer <API_KEY>. Static schema same for all callers; model selected via body \"model\". Streaming via SSE (\"stream\": true). Newer Responses API exists but chat/completions is canonical."
    },
    "dynamicscrm": {
      "connectorKey": "uipath-microsoft-dynamicscrm",
      "docsUrl": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-apps/developer/data-platform/webapi/reference/about?view=dataverse-latest",
      "dynamic": true,
      "notes": "Dataverse Web API, OData v4. Base path /api/data/v9.2/. Tenant-specific custom entities + custom columns; custom logical names carry publisher prefix (new_, cr123_), entity set pluralized in URL. $filter/$select/$expand. No $skip -> page via Prefer: odata.maxpagesize header + @odata.nextLink/$skiptoken; default cap 5000 rows. Lookups set via @odata.bind. Auth: Azure AD OAuth2, resource = org URL."
    },
    "datadog": {
      "connectorKey": "uipath-datadog-datadog",
      "docsUrl": "https://docs.datadoghq.com/api/latest/",
      "dynamic": false,
      "notes": "Site-specific host: api.datadoghq.com (US1), api.us3/us5.datadoghq.com, api.datadoghq.eu (EU1), api.ap1/ap2.datadoghq.com, api.ddog-gov.com. Wrong site 403s. Auth headers: DD-API-KEY (all), DD-APPLICATION-KEY (most read/scoped endpoints). Versioned paths /api/v1 and /api/v2 coexist. Pagination via page[cursor]/cursor params on v2."
    },
    "netsuite": {
      "connectorKey": "uipath-oracle-netsuite",
      "docsUrl": "https://docs.oracle.com/en/cloud/saas/netsuite/ns-online-help/book_1559132836.html",
      "dynamic": true,
      "notes": "SuiteTalk REST. Base https://<ACCOUNT_ID>.suitetalk.api.netsuite.com/services/rest. Records at /record/v1/<recordType>; SuiteQL at /query/v1/suiteql (POST, body {\"q\":...}, set Prefer: transient). Per-account custom fields prefixed custentity_/custbody_; custom record types custrecord_/customrecord_. Pagination limit/offset query params (max 1000/page), next via links. Auth: OAuth2 or token-based (TBA). Record schemas at system.netsuite.com REST_API_Browser."
    },
    "snowflake": {
      "connectorKey": "uipath-snowflake-snowflake",
      "docsUrl": "https://docs.snowflake.com/en/developer-guide/sql-api/reference",
      "dynamic": true,
      "notes": "Account-specific host https://<account_identifier>.snowflakecomputing.com/api/v2. POST /statements to run SQL; returns 202 + statementHandle if not finished -> poll GET /statements/{handle} until 200; cancel via POST /statements/{handle}/cancel. Async via ?async=true. Auth: Bearer JWT(key-pair)/OAuth. Large results partitioned. Tables/columns are tenant-defined -> schema not inferable from docs."
    },
    "github": {
      "connectorKey": "uipath-microsoft-github",
      "docsUrl": "https://docs.github.com/en/rest",
      "dynamic": false,
      "notes": "Base https://api.github.com. Set Accept: application/vnd.github+json and X-GitHub-Api-Version (default 2022-11-28). Pagination via Link header (rel=next/last) + per_page/page query params, NOT OData. No $filter; resource-specific query params. Fixed schema."
